      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Here is my assessment of last night's Beta for this spinning bug so far. In summary, there has been minor improvement, but it is still NOT FIXED or anywhere near the way it was before the late December 2018 update.\n\nHere is when spinning worked before the December 2018 update\nThe body always followed the head, and there were no spinning issues\nhttps://clips.twitch.tv/VibrantInspiringSpaghettiRiPepperonis\n\nHere is what it looked like when spinning broke for 9 months\nThe body doesn't follow the head when spinning. You have to reach your arms out or keep your head very still to avoid the issue, and even then it still happens.\nhttps://youtu.be/iGPQoR8hxh0?t=254\n\nHere is spinning with last night's Beta fixes.\nhttps://youtu.be/ikCKP_905ic?t=191\n\nIt's still not fixed or anywhere near the way it was before the December 2018 update.\n\nCompared to before the Beta, if we consciously try avoiding the spinning problem by moving our hands and head a certain way in the dance, it's easier than before the Beta to avoid the issue, but it still happens.\n\nAn easy way to see that it's still broken is bringing your arms in and doing a quick spin. It's harder to notice the problem while you're dancing because the body and head don't disconnect as long. It's really apparent in video though.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
